# SNIP architecture (this repository)

This repo is the first **SNIP domain application** (Network Planning & Optimisation), not the entire Simba Network Intelligence Platform.

Read before changing code:

- `docs/implementation/SNIP-IMPLEMENTATION-CONTEXT.md` (§0 is authoritative for scope)
- `docs/implementation/SNIP-IMPLEMENTATION-STATUS.md`
- `docs/implementation/SNIP-PHASE-1A.1-SEMANTIC-RAG-VALIDATION.md`

## Authorised now

Phase **1A.1** only: prove semantic RAG (real embeddings + vector retrieval + local LLM) while keeping the Phase 1A stub/lexical CI path.

```text
Documents + synthetic KPI → embed → vector retrieve → assemble → local LLM → cited recommendation → human
```

Default profile remains lexical + stub. `local-ai` uses Ollama (`nomic-embed-text`, `qwen2.5:7b`) and `SimpleVectorStore`.

## Do not implement

MCP, Agent Factory, autonomous agents, Kafka/MSK, EKS, Kong, ALB, ALICE, live gNB/network writes, RL, billing, Ionic, AWS lock-in, Phase 1B.

## Rules

- Extend Phase 1A abstractions (`ingest`, `retrieve`, `assemble`, `generate`). Do not rewrite the slice.
- Keep recommendations read-only. No apply/execute/write-to-network APIs.
- If retrieval is empty, do not fabricate citations.
- Ordinary CI must not download large models.
- Implementation markdown lives under `docs/implementation/`. ADRs under `docs/architecture/adr/`.
